---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Bread Engineer Support — Savoie Apps"
  description="Help, troubleshooting and contact details for Bread Engineer."
  canonicalUrl="https://savoie.app/apps/bread-engineer/support/"
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="app-info">
    <article class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Bread Engineer</p>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p class="lede">Need help with a recipe, fermentation estimate, timer, alarm, Live Activity or saved bake? Email us and we’ll help you get it sorted.</p>

      <a class="contact" href="mailto:support@savoie.app?subject=Bread%20Engineer%20Support%20Request">Email Bread Engineer support</a>

      <h2>Helpful details to include</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your Bread Engineer version and build number</li>
        <li>Your iPhone model and iOS version</li>
        <li>The recipe step you were using</li>
        <li>What you expected to happen and what happened instead</li>
        <li>A screenshot, if it helps explain the problem</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common fixes</h2>
      <h3>An alarm or notification did not appear</h3>
      <p>Open iOS Settings and confirm that Bread Engineer is allowed to show notifications and alarms. In Bread Engineer Settings, check that the alert types you want are enabled.</p>

      <h3>A timer is no longer visible</h3>
      <p>Open the active recipe and its current step. If a timer was interrupted by a device restart or permission change, start that step’s timer again.</p>

      <h3>A photo cannot be added</h3>
      <p>Check Bread Engineer’s Photos permission in iOS Settings, confirm there is free storage on the device, and try selecting the image again.</p>

      <h3>The fermentation estimate looks wrong</h3>
      <p>Check the dough and room conditions entered for the recipe. Fermentation timing is an equation-based estimate: flour, starter activity, temperature and technique can all affect the actual dough.</p>

      <p class="footnote">Bread Engineer is a planning aid, not a food-safety instrument. Observe your dough and use your judgement. See the <a href="/apps/bread-engineer/privacy/">Bread Engineer privacy policy</a> for data-handling details.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .app-info { padding: 4rem 0 5rem; }
  .app-info .container { max-width: 720px; }
  .eyebrow { margin: 0 0 .5rem; color: var(--color-primary); font-weight: 700; }
  h1 { margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 7vw, 3.75rem); letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .lede { max-width: 42rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: 1.12rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .contact { display: inline-block; margin: 1rem 0 2rem; padding: .8rem 1rem; border-radius: .8rem; background: var(--color-primary); color: white; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  h2 { margin: 2rem 0 .7rem; font-size: 1.3rem; }
  h3 { margin: 1.4rem 0 .35rem; font-size: 1rem; }
  p, li { line-height: 1.7; }
  li + li { margin-top: .35rem; }
  .footnote { margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text-secondary); font-size: .9rem; }
  .footnote a { color: var(--color-primary); }
</style>
